  "question": {
    "text": "The ratio of sigma and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#960;</mi></math> bonds present in pyrophosphoric acid is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "6",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>To determine the ratio of sigma and pi bonds in pyrophosphoric acid, we first need to understand the molecular structure of the compound.</p><p>Pyrophosphoric acid has the chemical formula <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>4</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>7</mn></msub></math>. The molecule contains two phosphorus atoms, seven oxygen atoms, and four hydrogen atoms.</p><p>The structure of pyrophosphoric acid is<br /><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/66a8fc03-a21b-4df2-8463-af37876b3c6d-image.png\" style=\"width: 300px; height: 144px;\" /></p><p>It contains total&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>12</mn></math>&nbsp;sigma bonds and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math>&nbsp;pi bonds. So<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mtext>&#160;No. of&#160;</mtext><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#963;</mi><mtext>&#160;bonds&#160;</mtext></mrow><mrow><mtext>&#160;No. of&#160;</mtext><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#960;</mi><mtext>&#160;bonds&#160;</mtext></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>12</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>:</mo><mn>1</mn></math></p></blockquote>",
    "image": null
  },
